SPOS-308
Title: Data sync system — outbox queue and five-layer fallback
Type: Task
Story Points: 13
Assignee: Backend Lead
Priority: Highest
Description: Build the complete data synchronisation system that moves completed day's data from the local store server to the Super Admin cloud dashboard. This is the most complex backend task in Phase 3. The system must implement all five fallback layers: real-time sync via outbox queue, auto-retry on failure, Z-Report forced retry, USB encrypted export, and catch-up sync on reconnection. All sync transmissions encrypted (TLS 1.3 in transit, AES-256 for USB export file). Sync status broadcast to dashboard via Reverb.
Implementation details:
Layer 1 — Outbox queue: every sale added to sync_outbox table on completion, background job picks up and sends to cloud API, marks as sent on 200 response
Layer 2 — Retry schedule: failed jobs retry at 1min, 5min, 15min, 30min intervals using Laravel exponential backoff
Layer 3 — Z-Report trigger: ZReportJob forces sync attempt for all pending outbox entries
Layer 4 — USB export: AES-256 encrypted .surapos file containing all pending days as JSON, importable via Super Admin Dashboard upload endpoint
Layer 5 — Catch-up: connectivity monitor pings every 60 seconds, on restore sends all pending outbox entries chronologically
Acceptance Criteria:

